      "capturedAt": "2026-06-28T01:05:12.974Z",
      "excerpt": "\"You and I\" is the debut single by R&B/funk musician Rick James, released in 1978 from his debut album, Come Get It!. It spent two weeks at number one on the Billboard R&B charts and reached number thirteen on the Billboard Hot 100. \"You and I\" also peaked at number three on the disco chart.\n\n\nPersonnel\nRick James - vocals, keyboards, synthesizers\nLevi Ruffin, Jr. - keyboards\nBilly Nunn – keyboards\nBobby Nunn – keyboards\nFreddie Rappilo – guitar\nAndy Rapillo – bass\nRichard Shaw – bass\nLorenzo Shaw – drums\nMike Caputy – drums\nRandy Jay Beckenstein (sax), Rick Bell (Trombone) and Mike Brecker – horns\nFlick (sax), Barry (trumpet), Steve Williams (trombone) - horns\nLevi and Jackie Ruffin, Bobby and Billy Nunn, Sascha Meeks, Richard Shaw, Vanessa Brooks Nunn, Joey Diggs, Anthony Ceasar, Roger Brown, Calvin Moore, Bennie McCullough - background vocals\nArt Stewart - co-producer\n\n\nReferences\n\n\nExternal links\nYou and I by Rick James at AllMusic",
      "confidence": 0.85,
